  "Question": "If \\(x\\lt-2\\) then \\(\\bigl|1-|1+x|\\bigr|\\) equals",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(2+x\\)",
    "B": "\\(-2-x\\)",
    "C": "\\(x\\)",
    "D": "\\(-x\\)",
    "E": "\\(-2\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "Work from the inside outward, using \\(|u|=-u\\) whenever \\(u<0\\). Since \\(x<-2\\), we have \\(1+x<-1<0\\), so\n\\[\n|1+x|=-(1+x)=-1-x.\n\\]\nIt follows that\n\\[\n1-|1+x|=1-(-1-x)=2+x.\n\\]\nThe condition \\(x<-2\\) also gives \\(2+x<0\\). Therefore,\n\\[\n\\bigl|1-|1+x|\\bigr|=|2+x|=-(2+x)=-2-x.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(-2-x\\), choice B.",
